nd{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={{field-1}}+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ {{field-2}}=-2{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+4{t}^{2}+2} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-2{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{t}^{2}}+2L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)}-4L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{8}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332814/field-1" "q-332814/field-2" "q-332814/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332814"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332825/field-1/85c6565ea814c9f2d620110aeaf3215e49bb282aeaa61df51feb3d4db26413d9" :answer/id #uuid "b80ea7bd-e565-5d92-8100-a82d25e9720c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332825/field-1/543e2480a1a957bff3396931ee6970882