 system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={{field-1}} \\\\ {{field-2}}=-3{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+6} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+6L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)}+L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the result\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332820/field-1" "q-332820/field-2" "q-332820/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332820"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332796/field-1/71bd365cc86cee3c0fd40b54658bbb282818e7d217849ae5dd8f4d0c035bbd24" :answer/id #uuid "caf90a76-2f6f-5525-ab34-ef461e92e158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332796/field-1/2688241f7cca1aadc105842f25be873f49f15807dad4258f5bf95eaafcb5b200" :answer/id #uuid "3d88f8c5-ca37-5408-b913-e80352562825" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332796/field-1/c6dd3ee18ac85ac02