7a6aaba944993b8057" :answer-field/choices ["q-332796/field-3/e95a22dcb48894635bdea7d6de08114e41918c20fa2ce07a6aaba944993b8057" "q-332796/field-3/689672a08b28fba294c58d7c7551b966529c1867da17fdb3ae1b4ced60fec7d8" "q-332796/field-3/952ee89c9a25ab49a2cb8ef75ac0b6b02bbe9f1573c257d1123d16d6e3926392" "q-332796/field-3/e5ce318969070c5bbd2d318a58ddf475c0b580b5cd39a2b6bdc8401ea491bfd5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332796" :question/id #uuid "690a42b8-dcb3-555a-9d9d-b596c97be14f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332796" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+3{t}^{2}+1} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{t}^{2}}+L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}-2L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL{1}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L{{t}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{6}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332796/field-1" "q-332796/field-2" "q-332796/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca890a8e-9ddd-51f7-9784-c9c1f020adef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332796"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333070/field-1/03abf6bd60989248337d878f02748181415560a91993e3e36b02f44d54a06971" :answer/id #uuid "bc960939-7466-5837-a3c8-8c2d9ec61bff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333070/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b249152-cd1c-5fa5-b2d9-815f8901e0be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333070/field-1/03abf6bd60989248337d878f02748181415560a91993e3e36b02f44d54a06971" :answer-field/choices ["q-333070/field-1/03abf6bd60989248337d878f02748181415560a91993e3e36b02f44d54a06971"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333070" :question/id #uuid "8e9610af-8627-5644-9e8a-233c67193c2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-333070" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{5{x}_{2}(t)+2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+3L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=5L{{x}_{2}(t)}+2L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =5{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{1}(s) & =3(\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-5)(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(s+2)}{s(s-2)(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s-5)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333070/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333064/field-1/4f991311b27a5ef0d4e25de21337633eab8076e57b80f56ee25b019c7eb071b5" :answer/id #uuid "3259fb49-8b62-5e7c-814c-5ccf996446b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-s^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333064/field-1/a46f81dfafbafaeaf233e58122922fc270e4bda621e46d603027a7c85dfc4e8f" :answer/id #uuid "952c48d0-e090-5c39-8ce5-360fe6a233ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164431 :answer-field/correct "q-333064/field-1/4f991311b27a5ef0d4e25de21337633eab8076e57b80f56ee25b019c7eb071b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-333064/field-1/4f991311b27a5ef0d4e25de21337633eab8076e57b80f56ee25b019c7eb071b5" "q-333064/field-1/a46f81dfafbafaeaf233e58122922fc270e4bda621e46d603027a7c85dfc4e8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-333064"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+4,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+4L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & ={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{2}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2(\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)})-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8}{s(s-3)}-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-{s}^{2}+3s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332784/field-1/7f13db7d0a276b6992a164eee26495cba75e903b2c4abc0b83461018cb6beeeb" :answer/id #uuid "4a32e5db-b9f5-505b-8d48-f944743b5a6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-s^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332784/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e21ff414-3cfb-5b40-98d0-9bb4ecb809be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332784/field-1/7f13db7d0a276b6992a164eee26495cba75e903b2c4abc0b83461018cb6beeeb" :answer-field/choices ["q-332784/field-1/7f13db7d0a276b6992a164eee26495cba75e903b2c4abc0b83461018cb6beeeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332784" :question/id #uuid "6458cb79-4630-59ec-b8b8-8020d6ba66c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-332784" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+5} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)})-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+5)-s(s+1)}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332784/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333071/field-1/caa205e7226b6dbe201b1d496dd488a0069d8324cafa371577851e0dd88d90e6" :answer/id #uuid "814838a9-e8b0-563c-86d9-7b7c56ae3169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333071/field-1/3931ae75e3c3b749dc3d058d2e3a788d3523ecf49a4b7c5ba3fe6c2ea1ca63d8" :answer/id #uuid "c90d6e72-1ef3-5a08-ab22-e39cf04b4ad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-7s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333071/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "195c2464-955c-5cf0-92f5-d81c249bcaef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333071/field-1/caa205e7226b6dbe201b1d496dd488a0069d8324cafa371577851e0dd88d90e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-333071/field-1/caa205e7226b6dbe201b1d496dd488a0069d8324cafa371577851e0dd88d90e6" "q-333071/field-1/3931ae75e3c3b749dc3d058d2e3a788d3523ecf49a4b7c5ba3fe6c2ea1ca63d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333071" :question/id #uuid "651a9779-f6de-5b80-8654-32c2c2209844" :question/math-academy-id "q-333071" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{2}(t)+6,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{4{x}_{2}(t)+6}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=4L{{x}_{2}(t)}+6L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{6}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-1+\\frac{6}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-s+6}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =2+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =2+(\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s(s-4)+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}-4s)+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-8s+6-s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s+3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-9s+6}{s(s-4)(s+3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{6-s}{s(s-4)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333071/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333071"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333073/field-1/a4019026796331505ca9bbcb5ce113394fbfe801be781858e29af987b6d94ae0" :answer/id #uuid "2be2015f-fdf1-586e-a915-01a2d0eeff2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333073/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2543f78-09cc-5180-a989-4e295efa12f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333073/field-1/a4019026796331505ca9bbcb5ce113394fbfe801be781858e29af987b6d94ae0" :answer-field/choices ["q-333073/field-1/a4019026796331505ca9bbcb5ce113394fbfe801be781858e29af987b6d94ae0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333073" :question/id #uuid "814d05ba-3fb8-5518-a28e-318cafedbdd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-333073" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{3{x}_{2}(t)+1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=4L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L{{x}_{2}(t)}+L{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)},$ and we have used the fact that $L{1}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =4{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =1+(\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-3)+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-3s+2s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-s+1}{s(s-3)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+1}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333073/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b22e449-2966-59cf-b012-3f5721b4bc98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333073"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330958/field-1/bdcb29dc13e558c3eaf1f5e5c9519400e6a377bfabfdc4b46018f3cd1b5b0e25" :answer/id #uuid "3252e5fc-04da-5d6a-8e94-ab4f44d532eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330958/field-1/a2e1990babe4fd624110ecd0856d1b60f2270cc84802631f09f5af3cecb335d0" :answer/id #uuid "762b5965-664d-54c8-bd85-59dde2c2eb85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164123 :answer-field/correct "q-330958/field-1/bdcb29dc13e558c3eaf1f5e5c9519400e6a377bfabfdc4b46018f3cd1b5b0e25" :answer-field/choices ["q-330958/field-1/bdcb29dc13e558c3eaf1f5e5c9519400e6a377bfabfdc4b46018f3cd1b5b0e25" "q-330958/field-1/a2e1990babe4fd624110ecd0856d1b60f2270cc84802631f09f5af3cecb335d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330958/field-2/ba75968afd6210aa2e5548f64ff216045b4a78979d17f135d8598265bfa965c9" :answer/id #uuid "22ca9c66-75ad-5618-ad0d-8205073d68c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}e^{t}-1+\\frac{3}{2}e^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164124 :answer-field/correct "q-330958/field-2/ba75968afd6210aa2e5548f64ff216045b4a78979d17f135d8598265bfa965c9" :answer-field/choices ["q-330958/field-2/ba75968afd6210aa2e5548f64ff216045b4a78979d17f135d8598265bfa965c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-330958"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+\\frac{3}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}+\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-333134/field-1/04661d30527741bfe4a65d119e50da9d3294788e77d16a242901c27c4baa7e75" :answer/id #uuid "e225d997-4bc4-5783-a5cb-3e279053bf13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e^{t}+e^{2t}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333134/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "67691548-2460-5ba8-a5ea-acc942e9ce8a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333134/field-1/04661d30527741bfe4a65d119e50da9d3294788e77d16a242901c27c4baa7e75" :answer-field/choices ["q-333134/field-1/04661d30527741bfe4a65d119e50da9d3294788e77d16a242901c27c4baa7e75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333134/field-2/e9fe93863772992148340a9838b688bf273c04331773e61b7a5ddea1e85e322f" :answer/id #uuid "f5b60664-c27a-5a0f-9f6e-bd7366469b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333134/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea061647-74da-5692-843a-8b2a00368435" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333134/field-2/e9fe93863772992148340a9838b688bf273c04331773e61b7a5ddea1e85e322f" :answer-field/choices ["q-333134/field-2/e9fe93863772992148340a9838b688bf273c04331773e61b7a5ddea1e85e322f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333134" :question/id #uuid "81391d77-04a8-59d4-9606-6ad64873b99c" :question/math-academy-id "q-333134" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}-2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333134/field-1" "q-333134/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333134"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333133/field-1/b1feaa643b5d931b7b02c1affd1c20e25ec5416f641328bd940ade3709af3dbb" :answer/id #uuid "310efa2f-7faf-5920-8172-91c6fd787af6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-t}+3e^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333133/field-1/e052b9c2ea851665a2aaf682942aac79108df614ae9abaa1c2ca19380c0c2cae" :answer/id #uuid "4f95e8f1-4539-5c94-8b5c-40e24f950755" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}+3e^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333133/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b71c073-9ac4-5ea6-b889-00e23e40dd27" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333133/field-1/b1feaa643b5d931b7b02c1affd1c20e25ec5416f641328bd940ade3709af3dbb" :answer-field/choices ["q-333133/field-1/b1feaa643b5d931b7b02c1affd1c20e25ec5416f641328bd940ade3709af3dbb" "q-333133/field-1/e052b9c2ea851665a2aaf682942aac79108df614ae9abaa1c2ca19380c0c2cae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333133/field-2/6270e768872c525a68b029965c20ec416d983196ef14899bec67f1e1254d25a5" :answer/id #uuid "92899a09-df9c-5618-8a98-b0e415f3a535" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{2t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333133/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1440bfec-292d-5009-bf1a-a3098f3c4fd1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333133/field-2/6270e768872c525a68b029965c20ec416d983196ef14899bec67f1e1254d25a5" :answer-field/choices ["q-333133/field-2/6270e768872c525a68b029965c20ec416d983196ef14899bec67f1e1254d25a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333133" :question/id #uuid "4af00dc3-1f8e-5a70-8450-3daf7f891fed" :question/math-academy-id "q-333133" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)+9 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}+3{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}+3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333133/field-1" "q-333133/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333137/field-1/d5031e8c26429d1f12424ffaf4caee265afacd7fefe66d6e14232430212f76db" :answer/id #uuid "0ad689f9-693a-5e23-bbf7-4914ad26c689" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e^{-2t}+3e^{t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333137/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "10ed8289-1747-5826-a3e7-724e9df91a76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333137/field-1/d5031e8c26429d1f12424ffaf4caee265afacd7fefe66d6e14232430212f76db" :answer-field/choices ["q-333137/field-1/d5031e8c26429d1f12424ffaf4caee265afacd7fefe66d6e14232430212f76db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333137/field-2/f9a648b00ef28dda6c3b0beebbabe0327b42ae1931a266802e3e070ce24139fa" :answer/id #uuid "789cf4dc-69d3-5290-acda-23900396e1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333137/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d01d122-8cbd-5a2c-b84e-f710648a0858" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333137/field-2/f9a648b00ef28dda6c3b0beebbabe0327b42ae1931a266802e3e070ce24139fa" :answer-field/choices ["q-333137/field-2/f9a648b00ef28dda6c3b0beebbabe0327b42ae1931a266802e3e070ce24139fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333137" :question/id #uuid "9b23ad7d-d82f-515a-9af4-4e7a337b8a30" :question/math-academy-id "q-333137" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)-20 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333137/field-1" "q-333137/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333137"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333138/field-1/a2c7d6b0cd4bd43fbff8b7f4e72c43d5fc127d49ae47d17404142c25e7fa3ace" :answer/id #uuid "4a351b36-7df6-5c3e-b421-2d95db069374" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e^{-t}+e^{2t}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333138/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4de10fb4-0149-5d55-8c06-47fdedc53f90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333138/field-1/a2c7d6b0cd4bd43fbff8b7f4e72c43d5fc127d49ae47d17404142c25e7fa3ace" :answer-field/choices ["q-333138/field-1/a2c7d6b0cd4bd43fbff8b7f4e72c43d5fc127d49ae47d17404142c25e7fa3ace"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333138/field-2/854e6d89b0c44dbce228e0af6db4eaa565556f17931b3df446d770d2067a8eda" :answer/id #uuid "c6bbce55-b4fa-5bff-a3d6-c1b20adb3449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333138/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c742fa95-6e63-5b34-a291-ffcbe7f6f572" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333138/field-2/854e6d89b0c44dbce228e0af6db4eaa565556f17931b3df446d770d2067a8eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-333138/field-2/854e6d89b0c44dbce228e0af6db4eaa565556f17931b3df446d770d2067a8eda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333138" :question/id #uuid "ce4553dc-a6b5-5c6c-a88c-0467c4bf99b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-333138" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{2}{s+1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1\\cdot t}+{e}^{2\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}-\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =-1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}+2-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ -1+{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333138/field-1" "q-333138/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff314a2-9059-5a37-8c2c-2b7a2fe6dcd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21575"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/assets/8161123eafa5ed80dc37b8e017c5598fcacaf241a84a09ca27f73d204d7b0e74.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, find the system of equations." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-3} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}-3L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}+2L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\cos(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{s}{s^2+4}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\sin(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{2}{s^2+4},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=2{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21576"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/assets/ce973be1a5a98fa04fad06c1ca5ee19c7f1b0cfd421d0cd449c7cb52138bf9bd.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$  find the solution of the new system." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+4} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{1} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}-3L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\},$ and we have used the fact that $\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac1s.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}) \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\dfrac{s+4}{s(s+1)} ,\\qquad \nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21577"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076259/assets/a699a4e262534557453aaa9e44d1b273dd4489190e50cec8f9ef9e0da91e7d29.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} = -\\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{2}{s-1} - \\dfrac{2}{s}, \\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." :question/worked-solution "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{2}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-1}}-2\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+2{e}^{1\\cdot t}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}+3\\,{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
